Hello!

Maybe this is a well-known anomaly, or maybe I am just confused.

When a list is the first thing after an \item command,
\@endparenv is not executed at the end of the list. This
means that the vertical space and penalty that
usually follow a list are not inserted.

Is there any reason for this?

I am appending a file which illustrates the effect
(and contains other junk for comparison).

It comes out the same with LaTeX and LaTeX2e.

Tim

